# Content Platform Architecture

- Treat novels, manga, and anime as separate media kinds in one shared publishing model.
- Do not overload `novels` tables or novel-only services to represent manga or anime.
- Add new creator publishing features behind additive tables, adapters, or new routes first.
- Preserve existing reading, watching, and library flows while the new platform is being introduced.
- Keep media metadata in relational tables and large binaries in object storage.
- Prefer reusable work, release, asset, and mint abstractions over medium-specific one-offs.
